<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Welcome to the second installment of our AWS Database Project series, focused on establishing real-world connectivity for our data infrastructure. In the previous part, we successfully provisioned a highly scalable and resilient Amazon Aurora relational database instance.)
/E (Welcome to the second installment of our AWS Database Project series, focused on establishing real-world connectivity for our data infrastructure. In the previous part, we successfully provisioned a highly scalable and resilient Amazon Aurora relational database instance.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This project, "AWS Aurora Database with Elastic Compute Cloud \(EC2\)," is the critical next step. The goal is to move beyond mere provisioning and create a functional application environment. The Aurora database, by design, is secured within a virtual private cloud \(VPC\) and isolated from the public internet. This step will demonstrate the professional, secure method for connecting an application server, simulated by an Amazon EC2 instance to the database, ensuring that our data is both accessible to our application code and protected from unauthorized external access.)
/E (This project, "AWS Aurora Database with Elastic Compute Cloud \(EC2\)," is the critical next step. The goal is to move beyond mere provisioning and create a functional application environment. The Aurora database, by design, is secured within a virtual private cloud \(VPC\) and isolated from the public internet. This step will demonstrate the professional, secure method for connecting an application server, simulated by an Amazon EC2 instance to the database, ensuring that our data is both accessible to our application code and protected from unauthorized external access.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (By the end of this module, you will have a complete, secure backend stack where your application logic runs on a dedicated EC2 server, interacting seamlessly with the powerful Aurora database, ready for deployment and scaling.)
/E (By the end of this module, you will have a complete, secure backend stack where your application logic runs on a dedicated EC2 server, interacting seamlessly with the powerful Aurora database, ready for deployment and scaling.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
